<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all padding="0" />
      <mj-text font-family="sans-serif" />
      <mj-class name="header" padding="10px 10px 20px 10px" background-color="white" />
      <mj-class name="header-title" align="left" font-family="monospace" font-size="24pt" font-weight="600" line-height="24pt" padding-bottom="10px" />
      <mj-class name="header-image" align="right" width="100px" />
      <mj-class name="header-issue" align="left" font-family="monospace" font-weight="200" />
      <mj-class name="header-date" align="right" font-family="monospace" font-weight="200" />

      <mj-class name="article" padding-bottom="10px" />
      <mj-class name="article-title" font-family="monospace" font-weight="400" font-size="14pt" />

      <mj-class name="summary" padding="0 10px 20px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="category-heading" font-family="monospace" font-weight="600" font-size="18pt" />

      <mj-class name="articles" padding="0 10px 0 10px" />
      <mj-class name="images" padding="0 10px 20px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="footer" padding="10px 10px 10px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="footer-unsub" align="left" />
      <mj-class name="footer-feedback" align="right" />
    </mj-attributes>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body>
    <mj-container>

      <!-- Header -->
      <mj-wrapper mj-class="header">
        <mj-section>
          <mj-column width="100%" vertical-align="middle">
            <mj-text mj-class="header-title">Newsletter del Lunes.</mj-text>
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-group>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="header-issue">Issue No. 31</mj-text>
            </mj-column>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="header-date">16 Junio 2025</mj-text>
            </mj-column>
          </mj-group>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-column>
            <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-style="dotted" border-color="lightgrey" />
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>
      </mj-wrapper>
      <!-- /Header -->

      <!-- Summary -->
      <mj-section mj-class="summary">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text>
            
Buenas a todos,
</br></br>
En esta edición hablaremos sobre la importancia de saber decir que no en el ámbito profesional, cómo el valor que aportamos puede ir más allá de nuestras habilidades técnicas, un interesante video sobre Clean Code presentado en el OpenSouthCode, y un artículo técnico sobre el uso correcto de hilos en Qt.
</br></br>
Un saludo!

          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <!-- Images -->
      <mj-section mj-class="images">
        <mj-column>
          
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>
      
      <mj-section>
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text>
            <h2>Artículos</h2>
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <!-- Articles -->
			<mj-wrapper mj-class="articles">
				
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/cuando-agradar-es-ser-profesional-braulio-diez-botella-ehxbe/">Cuando agradar no es ser profesional</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">A veces, hay que saber cuando decir que no, hay muchas maneras y situaciones, pero tenemos que aprender a valorar cuando podemos decir si y cuando no.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://medium.com/realworld-ai-use-cases/why-clients-pay-me-10x-more-than-developers-who-are-better-at-coding-than-me-10bc46f6e67b">Why clients pay me 10x more than developers who are better at coding than me | by Chris Dunlop | Realworld AI Use Cases | Jun, 2025 | Medium</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Cambia cliente por Jefe de proyecto, y el efecto es lo mismo pero dentro de la empresa.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://youtu.be/TTCugqSuJn8">Clean code, ¿de verdad vale la pena? - Jonathan Vila - OpenSouthCode 2023 - YouTube [video] </a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Video sobre Clean Code del OpenSouthCode del año pasado.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://www.vikingsoftware.com/how-to-use-qthread-properly/">How to use QThread properly - Viking Software A/S</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Volvemos un poquito con Qt, artículo de empresa que les gusta mucho publicar sobre Qt explicando como usar los hilos de Qt correctamente..</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        

        
      </mj-wrapper>

      <!-- Footer -->
      <mj-wrapper mj-class="footer">
        <mj-section>
          <mj-column>
            <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-style="dotted" border-color="lightgrey" padding-bottom="5px" />
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-group>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="footer-unsub">Not interested? <a href="mailto:daniel.agredano@gtd.eu?Subject=iX%20Newsletter%20--%20Unsubscribe">Unsubscribe</a></mj-text>
            </mj-column>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="footer-feedback"><a href="mailto:daniel.agredano@gtd.eu?Subject=iX%20Newsletter%20--%20Feedback">Feedback</a></mj-text>
            </mj-column>
          </mj-group>
        </mj-section>
      </mj-wrapper>

    </mj-container>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
